11	/**
12	 * See it and hear it, then say its tones: the Thai word is shown and its
13	 * pronunciation played together on mount — there is no "hear it" vs. "see
14	 * it" split here, because the question is neither the spelling nor the
15	 * meaning but the word's tone pattern, and both halves of the prompt are
16	 * needed to answer it (`ToneChallengeDirection` has one value for exactly
17	 * this reason). The reveal shows every syllable beside its tone and the
18	 * learner self-rates whether they identified the whole pattern.
